\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Schematic illustration of the three fundamental classes of magnetic order: ferromagnetism, antiferromagnetism, and altermagnetism. Ferromagnets exhibit a net magnetization due to the parallel alignment of spins, while conventional antiferromagnets have zero net magnetization due to antiparallel alignment of spins on different sublattices. Altermagnets also have zero net magnetization but feature a unique momentum-dependent spin splitting of the electronic bands, arising from their distinct symmetry properties. \cite  {Song2025}}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
